se cards as efficiently as possible. I\'ve got a mixed bag: triples (555, 777, AAA), pairs (88, JJ, KK), and a smattering of singles (3, 6, Q, 2, Black Joker). The strength here lies in those triples and the control cards (2 and BJ). My immediate thought is to create a structure that uses these strengths while eliminating weaknesses.\n\nThe key is realizing that 555 and 777 are vulnerable to higher triples. AAA is a beast, but I don\'t want to burn it too early. I\'m focusing on getting rid of the low cards while retaining control.\n\nMy hand analysis points to a "triples with singles" strategy. It allows me to combine triples and singles. Since I have three triples (555, 777, AAA) and three weak singles (3, 6, Q), it seems that these can be used very quickly.\n\nI\'m leaning towards opening with `555+3`. Clearing those two cards means I have to react less to potential counters and sets up my remaining hands with pairs and single top cards (2 and BJ) for control.\n\nIt leaves me with the following cards: 6, 777, 88, JJ, Q, KK, AAA, 2, BJ.\n\nMy plan then is to get rid of my 777+6. Then, I need to use the AAA, ideally to force a response. I can use the 2 or BJ to close out the hand with my pairs. It\'s a solid strategy to create a powerful endgame.\n\nLet\'s check card counting for a moment. With my current cards, I know what is in hand, but I don\'t know what is gone. Therefore, any move now can risk being beaten easily by someone who has an early bomb or high trip. I\'ve got to take that risk.\n\nConsidering all the options, playing `555+3` seems like the most logical and structurally sound opening move.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The hand contains three triples (555, 777, AAA), three pairs (88, JJ, KK), and five singles (3, 6, Q, 2, Black Joker). The most efficient strategy is to play the "Triplets with attached single" pattern. I have three low/mid singles (3, 6, Q) that perfectly match the three triples. Playing the pairs as kickers would leave me with 5 disjointed singles, which is a very weak structure. By playing 555+3, I clear my lowest cards while preserving the strong structure of pairs and high control cards (2, Black Joker, AAA).\n\nReason: Opening with the lowest Triple with Single (555 + 3) optimizes the hand structure by utilizing the weak single \'3\'. This sets up a game plan to play 777+6 and AAA+Q subsequently, leaving a strong endgame of three pairs (88, JJ, KK) and two major control cards (2, Black Joker). I also hold blocking cards (pairs of J and K) which makes it harder for opponents to dominate the triple plays.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠3", "♠5", "♣5", "♦5"]}'}
